[{"source": "security", "severity": "note", "category": "coverage-gap", "title": "fold-check never compares the new tick-1 to the blessed manifest despite its documented 'cross-checked' claim", "location": "harness/fold_check.odin:12-13,55-66", "evidence": "// under the CURRENT catalogs, FNV's it (the NEW tick-1 — cross-checked against\n// the blessed manifest), splices the PREVIOUS hash at the fold position ... \tnew_tick1 := pp.fnv1a64(dump) ... \tfmt.printfln(\"fold-check: new tick-1        %016x  (the blessed manifest must match)\", new_tick1)\n\tfmt.printfln(\"fold-check: spliced prev      %016x  (must equal the prev tick-1)\", spliced_hash)\n\tif spliced_hash == prev_tick1_u {", "detail": "The only programmatic equality check is spliced_hash == prev_tick1_u; the new tick-1 is print-only, so the header's 'cross-checked against the blessed manifest' relies on the operator's eyes. Risk is bounded: harness run still compares T1 hashes.", "recommended_fix": "In run_fold_check, parse goldens/boot.t1 and fail (exit 1) when new_tick1 differs from its tick-1 line, making the printed cross-check programmatic instead of manual."}]
